I finish my tea and leave the stall.
The market is still very crowded.
I walk towards my building.
My cloth bags are heavy now.
There are fresh tomatoes and bananas in them.
I also have the fragrant tea masala.
I am feeling very good today.
Now I easily ask, "How much is this?"
I understand the numbers and prices properly.
I have a lot of confidence in myself today.
My building is just a short distance away.
I go inside the gate.
I need to put the marigold garland on my door.
Then I have to cook dinner.
I need the fresh tomatoes for dinner.
I am very happy with my shopping.
I am slowly settling into this life in Mumbai.
